    "title": "STRING PPI network of DE-regulated proteins (mouse) \u2014 largest connected component",
    "caption": "Protein-protein interaction network from STRING v12.0 (species=10090, Mus musculus, required_score=400) built from the 715 DE-\"regulated\" seed proteins (206 UP, 509 DOWN; |log2FC|>=0.585). 694/715 seeds (97.1%) mapped to a STRING identifier, yielding a 694-node / 5963-edge network with 57 greedy-modularity communities. Only the largest connected component (645 nodes, 5960 edges) is drawn for legibility; 49 nodes across 46 smaller components are omitted. Node color = log2 fold change (blue = down, red = up); node size is proportional to STRING degree; the top 15 hub genes by degree are labeled. IMPORTANT: this is an exploratory network over the hypothesis-generating |log2FC|>=0.585 candidate set from an n=2 technical-replicate SILAC design (no biological replication) in which 0/1938 proteins pass FDR<0.05 (limma) \u2014 network structure reflects STRING's curated evidence, not statistical significance in this dataset, and should not be read as confirmed findings.",
